  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 2.6,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.97,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings roughly doubled every hour from 1 to 5 h, then stopped suddenly at about 0.75–0.77. That sudden flat line looks like the reader topping out rather than the culture reaching stationary phase. I tested this on retained aliquots. The 18 h aliquot read 0.2611 and 0.2667 at 10x dilution, which corresponds to an OD of about 2.64. At 20x it read 0.1338 and 0.1235, about 2.57. The two dilutions agree after correction, so the diluted readings are in the reader's proportional range. Both are about 3.4 times the undiluted 18 h reading of 0.752. The 12 h aliquot at 10x read 0.2627 and 0.2523, about 2.58, against an undiluted reading of 0.777. So the culture was already above 2.5 by 12 h and stayed at about 2.6 through 18 h. The undiluted values from about 5–6 h onward are capped by the reader and understate biomass. Estimated OD600 at 18 h: about 2.6."
  },
